<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gibraltar</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gibraltar is a rocky promontory at the southern tip of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a>, commanding the strait between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> and the Atlantic. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravid Empire</a> crossed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strait-of-gibraltar">Strait of Gibraltar</a> in 1086 to intervene in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> gained Gibraltar through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-utrecht">Treaty of Utrecht</a> in 1713, holding it as a strategic base of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gibraltar.jpg" alt="Gibraltar" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Created on behalf of Isabella I of Castile in 1502; this version uploaded by Denelson83 (talk · contribs) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Gibraltar.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
